**How to implement.** What a picked lab file's bytes suggest, and the preview of its first rows, for the wizard (001 §K 'sniff the delimiter, header and BOM, and show a preview'; 001 §O 'Data dialog: preview, column roles, an import-profile picker'; the S9.2 brief: 'sniffing'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, after `LabFileSource` (step 132): `type FileByteContent with` (`Softellect.Sys.Primitives.FileByteContent`, STL `Sys/Primitives.fs`) `member this.kitFileText : KitFileText`, the bytes decoded as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark (EF BB BF) dropped, and `member this.byteOrderMark : ByteOrderMark`, `ByteOrderMarkPresent` when the bytes start with that mark. Every decode of a kit's bytes with a leading mark dropped calls `kitFileText`: the reads and copy-in of `KitProxy.create` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs`, steps 126-128, 133) and the copy-in of `KitProxy.createInMemory` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs`, step 133), their own decode bodies deleted, so one decode remains and every text they answer is unchanged. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, after `ColumnRoles.tryOfChoices`: `LabFileSniff = { bom : ByteOrderMark; delimiter : DataDelimiter; header : HeaderRowChoice }`, what a file's first lines suggest; `PreviewCell of string` with `.value`; `PreviewRow of PreviewCell list` with `member this.cells : PreviewCell list`; `LabFilePreview = { columnNames : PreviewCell list; rows : PreviewRow list }`, a file's columns and first rows as a layout reads them; and `type LabFileSource with member this.sniffedLayout : LabFileSniff`: the mark is `content.byteOrderMark`; over the first ten non-empty lines of `content.kitFileText` (each trimmed of a `\r`), the delimiter is the first of `DataDelimiter.all` whose character splits every one of them into the same number of at least two cells, `CommaDelimiter` when none does; the header is `HeaderOnFirstRow` when the first line, split so, has no cell that `Double.TryParse` with `NumberStyles.Float` and `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture` reads, or has a cell that does not read where the second line's cell of that position does, and `NoHeaderRow` otherwise. It is a suggestion the wizard shows and the user changes (step 308); it touches no disk. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs`: `type KitFileText with member this.previewWith (delimiter : DataDelimiter) (header : HeaderRowChoice) : Result<LabFilePreview, ExperimentDataError>`, through step 302's private CSV read, so the preview shows the cells a mapping reads: the column names are the header's trimmed cells, or `Column <n>` for each column of the widest of the first twenty rows when there is no header; the rows are the first twenty data rows' cells; an empty text is `EmptyDataFileErr`, and the read's error passes through. No cache, encoding guess or other member is added. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` (step 300) gains `sniffing suggests the delimiter, the header and the byte-order mark of a lab file`: a `LabFileSource` of the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,1,2026-07-15T12:05:00+00:00,45,912.25\n` sniffs `ByteOrderMarkPresent`, `CommaDelimiter` and `HeaderOnFirstRow`, and its `content.kitFileText` starts `experiment,` with no mark; `0;1.5\n20;1.25\n` sniffs `ByteOrderMarkAbsent`, `SemicolonDelimiter` and `NoHeaderRow`; `phi\tI\n0\t0.5\n` sniffs `TabDelimiter` and `HeaderOnFirstRow`; and `one column\n` sniffs `CommaDelimiter` and `HeaderOnFirstRow`. `LabFileImportTests` (step 301) gains `the preview shows a lab file's columns and first rows as the mapping reads them`: the Phone ROI text of step 303 previewed by comma with a header shows the five column names and its two rows; with `NoHeaderRow` it shows `Column 1` to `Column 5` and three rows, the header among them; a text of thirty data rows shows twenty. `KitProxyTests`' byte-order-mark facts (steps 128, 133, 204) pass unchanged. Verification (claim-check repair, .spec-md §9): ui-tests MUST select OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests (Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:FsxAcceptanceTests) to preserve the constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples. The constructor-unit-tests behavior checks above remain required; this selection neither edits that class nor substitutes for the future kit-acceptance tests.

**Acceptance.** After sniffing and the preview land, `LabFileSource.sniffedLayout` MUST suggest a picked file's byte-order mark, delimiter and header, `KitFileText.previewWith` MUST show its columns and first twenty rows through the reader the mappings use, and `FileByteContent.kitFileText` MUST be the kit's one decode; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `sniffing suggests the delimiter, the header and the byte-order mark of a lab file` and `the preview shows a lab file's columns and first rows as the mapping reads them`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass. ui-tests MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests, preserving its constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples and its test count.
